A king wants to build \( n \) cities and connect them with \( n-1 \) roads in such a way that any city can be reached from any other city (each road connects two cities, and roads do not intersect or pass through other cities). The king demands that the shortest distances between pairs of cities along the road network should be exactly 1 km, 2 km, 3 km, $\cdots, \frac{n(n-1)}{2}$ km. Determine if the king's requirement can be met for the cases:
(1) \( n = 6 \);
(2) \( n = 1986 \).

Let the function $f(x)=|2x+3|-|2x-a|$, where $a\in\mathbb{R}$.

$(1)$ If the solution set of the inequality $f(x)\leqslant -5$ is non-empty, find the range of values for the real number $a$;

$(2)$ If the graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is symmetric about the point $\left(-\dfrac{1}{2},0\right)$, find the value of the real number $a$.

Square $ABCD$ has side length $s$, a circle centered at $E$ has radius $r$, and $r$ and $s$ are both rational. The circle passes through $D$, and $D$ lies on $\overline{BE}$. Point $F$ lies on the circle, on the same side of $\overline{BE}$ as $A$. Segment $AF$ is tangent to the circle, and $AF=\sqrt{9+5\sqrt{2}}$. What is $r/s$?

[asy]
pair A,B,C,D,I,F;
A=(0,10); B=(0,0); C=(10,0); D=(10,10);

I=(14,13); F=(11,17);
draw(A--B--C--D--cycle,linewidth(0.7));
draw(Circle(I,5),linewidth(0.7));
draw(A--F,linewidth(0.7));
label("$A$",A,NW);
label("$B$",B,SW);
label("$C$",C,SE);
label("$D$",D,SW);
label("$F$",F,N);
label("$E$",I,E);
dot(I);
[/asy]The answer is in the form  rac{m}{n}, where gcd(m, n) = 1. Please provide the value of m + n.

