(Ⅱ) When the number of students is what, the charges by the two travel agencies are the same;  
(Ⅲ) Discuss which travel agency is more cost-effective based on the number of students $x$.

How many triangles are in the figure below, where the structure consists of a square grid of dots with 3 rows and 3 columns, and triangles are formed by connecting these dots?
[asy]
defaultpen(linewidth(0.7));
for(int i=0; i<3; ++i) {
    for(int j=0; j<3; ++j) {
        dot((i,j));
        if(i < 2) {
            draw((i,j)--(i+1,j)); // horizontal lines
        }
        if(j < 2) {
            draw((i,j)--(i,j+1)); // vertical lines
        }
        if(i < 2 && j < 2) {
            draw((i,j)--(i+1,j+1)); // diagonal lines
            draw((i+1,j)--(i,j+1)); // cross diagonal
        }
    }
}
[/asy]

